  "summary_en": "Ray Trace casts rays from a per-pixel origin and direction map against input geometry, and reports the first hit with its position and geometric normal. It can bake maps such as occlusion, cavity, curvature, thickness, edge and rounded normal by tracing secondary rays, and it can write geometry attribute values at each hit into output layers. The page does not state its internal name; the Copernicus index links raytrace.html.",
